# Binance MCP & Agent OS Rules

## Official Endpoint

- MCP Server: `https://agent.binance.com/mcp/agentic`
- Prefer the official Binance MCP over third-party wrappers when possible.

## Key Constraints

- All trading activity must target the **Agentic sub-account** only.
- No external withdrawals are allowed through this system.
- Market data can be public (no auth). Account and trading scopes require user authorization.
- Always respect the scopes the user actually granted.

## Patterns to Follow

- Follow Binance precision rules for quantities and prices.
- Use proper order types (LIMIT, MARKET, etc.) as supported by the MCP.
- Handle rate limits and transient errors gracefully.
- Never assume the sub-account is funded — check balances before proposing size.

## Skills Hub

When richer context is needed (token info, smart-money, audits), prefer installing and using:

```bash
npx skills add https://github.com/binance/binance-skills-hub
```

Reference Skills Hub skills instead of reinventing market data fetching when appropriate.
